      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that VMA readahead doesn\u0027t start in 4KB processes today: since aosp/4379310 restores the sibling slices that share the faulting swap entry, a sequential pass faults once per kernel page, so `__swapin_nr_pages()` never sees adjacent 4KB offsets and the window stays at one page. Could the message say that, rather than only that it \"selects the wrong window\"?\n\nAs far as I can see, `swap_vma_readahead_p3s` from aosp/4367986 checks exactly this (page 10 read ahead after faults on native pages 8 and 9), so it fails until this patch and could follow it when aosp/4367986 is split.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "78933fa15e3631453ff5d73a2061c25099c745d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
