        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T20:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this stays, would you mind moving the 4KB window into a helper in `include/linux/p3s/swap.h` (inside its existing `#if` block, with a stub in the `#else` branch), so that `swap_vma_ra_win()` keeps upstream\u0027s window code and only gains a hook after the `win \u003d\u003d 1` check? Something like:\n\n```\n\tif (vma_is_p3s_4k(vma))\n\t\treturn p3s_swap_vma_ra_win(vma, faddr, prev_faddr, win, start, end);\n```\n\nThe history then only needs `__swapin_nr_pages()` to count kernel pages (`prev_faddr \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL` and `faddr \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL`), which is what `PFN_DOWN()` already gives native VMAs. That keeps the geometry comment, the new locals and the unit math out of `mm/swap_state.c`, so upstream changes there don\u0027t conflict with P3S.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "78933fa15e3631453ff5d73a2061c25099c745d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "85668b2b_fe8b2b8c",
        "filename": "mm/swap_state.c",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 719,
