        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T20:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure readahead is wanted in 4KB processes, though. On `SWP_SYNCHRONOUS_IO` devices such as zram, `do_swap_page()` skips the swap cache and readahead when the swap count is 1, as for unshared native pages, while a folio mapped by several 4KB slices holds one swap reference per slice PTE, so its swap-in goes through `swapin_readahead()`.\n\nWith this change, 4KB processes would read ahead from zram where native processes don\u0027t (with `page-cluster` at 0, `swap_vma_ra_win()` returns before any of this). Is there a workload that needs it? If not, would it be OK to drop this patch, together with `swap_vma_readahead_p3s`?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "78933fa15e3631453ff5d73a2061c25099c745d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d2c044ba_c895594b",
        "filename": "mm/swap_state.c",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 726,
