        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T20:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the walk can now read the faulting folio through one of its sibling slices. When the fault isn\u0027t on the first slice, the window starts at or before its kernel page, so `swap_vma_readahead()` reaches the earlier slices first. They hold the same swap entry, so `__read_swap_cache_async()` allocates the target folio there with `addr !\u003d vmf-\u003eaddress`, which marks it `PG_readahead` and counts it as `SWAP_RA` although `do_swap_page()` maps it right away.\n\nCould that check compare `entry.val !\u003d targ_entry.val` instead? Native VMAs wouldn\u0027t change, since only the faulting PTE normally holds `targ_entry` there.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "78933fa15e3631453ff5d73a2061c25099c745d6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
