      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T20:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this hunk doesn\u0027t change anything: this file opts into `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, arm64 derives `PMD_SHIFT` from the per-process `PAGE_SHIFT`, and `swap_vma_readahead()` calls this under `P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM(vmf-\u003evma-\u003evm_mm)` since aosp/4312500. So `PMD_MASK` and `PMD_SIZE` are already 2MB for a 4KB mm, the same as `mm_pmd_size(mm)`.\n\nWould it be OK to keep upstream\u0027s two lines and drop the `mm` and `pmd_mask` locals, along with \"bounded by the target mm\u0027s PMD size\" in the message?",
